---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | LocalPDF';
const description = 'Read the LocalPDF Privacy Policy, including what data we collect, how billing and analytics work, and how to contact us.';
const canonical = 'https://localpdf.online/privacy';
const image = 'https://localpdf.online/og/home.svg';
const privacySchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: title,
  description,
  url: canonical,
};
---

<MarketingLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} image={image} schema={privacySchema}>
  <div class="page-shell legal-shell">
    <section class="section intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="section-intro">
        This Privacy Policy explains what personal data LocalPDF may process, why we process it, and how to contact us about privacy requests.
      </p>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: 2026-03-22</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">1. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions, data access requests, deletion requests, or billing-related data questions, contact
        <a href="mailto:support@localpdf.online">support@localpdf.online</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">2. What LocalPDF does</h2>
      <p>
        LocalPDF is a local-first PDF product. Many core document actions are designed to run in the browser rather than through an upload-first workflow.
        However, the website still uses normal web infrastructure, and some product functions rely on external services such as payment processing,
        analytics, hosting, and license validation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because of that, LocalPDF should not be understood as “collects nothing.” Instead, we aim to keep data collection limited, practical, and aligned with
        the actual product behavior.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">3. Data we may process</h2>
      <ul class="bullet-list">
        <li><strong>Billing data:</strong> purchase records, subscription status, transaction metadata, and license-related identifiers processed through LemonSqueezy.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser type, device information, page requests, timestamps, referrers, and basic server logs.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics data:</strong> usage events and website behavior if analytics tools are enabled.</li>
        <li><strong>Support data:</strong> messages you send to us, including your email address and any information you choose to include.</li>
        <li><strong>License restore data:</strong> submitted license keys, validation responses, and related anti-abuse or rate-limit metadata.</li>
        <li><strong>Local storage data:</strong> browser-side tokens or settings required to remember your billing state or product preferences.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">4. Document handling</h2>
      <p>
        Many LocalPDF workflows are built around local browser processing. That means documents do not always need to be uploaded to a remote processing backend
        just to begin a task.
      </p>
      <p>
        Still, you should not assume that every part of the broader site experience is entirely local. Billing, analytics, restore requests, support, and normal web
        hosting can involve network requests and third-party processors.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">5. Why we process data</h2>
      <ul class="bullet-list">
        <li>To operate, secure, and improve the website and app</li>
        <li>To process payments and manage subscriptions</li>
        <li>To restore and validate Pro access</li>
        <li>To prevent abuse, fraud, and technical misuse</li>
        <li>To understand product usage and improve user experience</li>
        <li>To respond to support requests and legal obligations</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">6. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>LocalPDF may use third-party providers, including categories such as:</p>
      <ul class="bullet-list">
        <li><strong>Payments and subscriptions:</strong> LemonSqueezy</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics and measurement:</strong> tools such as Google Analytics, PostHog, or Vercel Analytics when enabled</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting and delivery:</strong> website hosting, CDN, and infrastructure providers</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers may process personal data according to their own policies and contractual roles.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">7. Cookies, analytics, and local storage</h2>
      <p>
        The website and app may use cookies, local storage, or similar browser technologies to support analytics, billing state, feature behavior, and basic site
        functionality.
      </p>
      <p>
        If analytics tooling is enabled, your interactions with the site may be measured in aggregate or event form to help improve the product.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">8. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain data for as long as reasonably necessary to operate the service, comply with legal obligations, prevent abuse, resolve disputes, and support billing
        records. Different categories of data may be retained for different periods depending on legal, operational, and security needs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">9. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on your location, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection, or portability of personal data.
        To make a request, email <a href="mailto:support@localpdf.online">support@localpdf.online</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">10. International processing</h2>
      <p>
        LocalPDF and its providers may process data in multiple countries depending on hosting, payment, and analytics infrastructure. By using the service,
        you understand that data may be processed outside your home jurisdiction.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section legal-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">11. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The latest version will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section final-band">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Related pages</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Need the policy pages tied together?</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Read Terms for service boundaries and Refund Policy for cancellation, refunds, and subscription questions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/terms">Read Terms</a>
        <a class="btn-secondary" href="/refund-policy">Read Refund Policy</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .legal-shell {
    max-width: 940px;
  }

  .intro h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 5vw, 4.8rem);
    margin-top: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .meta {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .legal-section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .final-band {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
  }
</style>
